                            vpiDecompile: "\"Warning: [Unisim %s-1] BISC Calibration : DELAY_FORMAT set to TIME with EN_VTC signal set to 0. In hardware, when the EN_VTC signal is low during the initial calibration process, the BISC will never complete and the DLY_RDY and VTC_RDY status signals from the BITSLICE_CONTROL remain low. Simulation will not reflect this behavior. In simulation, the DLY_RDY and VTC_RDY from the BITSLICE_CONTROL will assert high. You should ensure the EN_VTC signal is held high during initial BISC self calibration to ensure BISC completes in hardware. See Select IO Userguide UG571 for more information.Instance: %m\""
